on-arrival: workers_spd += 8*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 8*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 8*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 4*(1-dissent); rural_spd += 4*(1-dissent); catholics_spd += 1*(1-dissent); reformist_dissent -= 5; reformist_strength += 5; left_dissent += 5; left_strength -= 5; center_dissent += 5; center_strength -= 5; labor_dissent -= 5; labor_strength += 5; neorevisionist_dissent -= 10 if neorevisionism; neorevisionist_strength += 10 if neorevisionism; socialism += 2*(1 - dissent); nationalism -= 6*(1 - dissent); bdf_cooperation = 1;

We cooperate with ***Bund Deutscher Frauenvereine*** to hold extensive campaigns, promoting women's rights at work at home, seeking to offer a common ground to both "traditional" and "new" women. We make accent on the livelihoods of widows and mothers who have lost their family in the Great War, those women who belong to the working poor, and aim to shift the blame in the popular perception of domestic abuse from influence of alcohol to present power imbalances.

While some prominent conservative activists, like Annagrete Lehmann, oppose our efforts out of a principle, even the most traditional women have grievances our rhetoric can appeal to.

(We can now sponsor BDF campaigns.)

@deny

We are a party of the working class, and we do not have a responsibility to show preferential treatment.
